A||||7||Adrift||Rear Lights - where do the wires come from?||||5||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-16-2001||09:12 PM||||Strange question: When I got my fiero it had no body on it (was gona be used for a kit car donor). Although the wiring in the front is connected properly into the car, some of the wires comming out of it are just cut and hanging. <P><BR>I was given the wiring for the rear lights with the car as well, but they were cut clean from the car as well, and i don't know where they're supposed to go.<P>Does the wiring for the rear lights come out of the same socket in the hood of the car as the wiring for the front lights? If so, How does the wiring get from the front of the car to the back?<P>If anyone has pics that would be great, I'll try to get some pictures later tonight to better explain my predictament.<P>Thanks<BR>Ari<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||11-17-2001||01:10 AM||||No, the wiring for the rear lights comes off of the junction block on the left rear engine bay wall......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-17-2001||01:16 AM||||Ah damn, does that mean I'll have to connect each individual wire seperatly! Ahh!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||11-17-2001||01:17 AM||||do the wires come out of the engine compartment and run on the outside of the body to the back, or under the car, or what?||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||11-17-2001||04:19 AM||||They run out from the engine compartment, down the right side, across the back and terminate on the left side (for the right marker light)||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||11-17-2001||08:18 AM||||Ari    If you want to save some time, you can find another rear harness from the junction box back.  Will save considerable soldering.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000006||revin||11-17-2001||09:59 AM||||After a fire,I had to rewire the whole car! 1st get the correct harness from the same year fiero! I bought one from a 86 or 87 for my 88.Wrong! I thought I could cut and splice with no problem(blue to blue and red to red). Wrong!  There were several of the same colors!!So I got the whole thing from connector to connector. I still had to move/switch some wires around in the wire block. That took a little time! I could not have done it with out a wire diagram from my manual!<BR>Hint: If you will be planing on adding accessories (extra,fan,foglites,special secret switches,etc.) run the wire now and include them in the wire harness! It will save you time down the road!! trust me!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Adrift||11-17-2001||10:11 AM||||Thanks, I think I'll just grab myself another wiring harness<BR>Ari<BR>||||reg||1
